just is a command runner for saving and executing project-specific
commands. Recipes are stored in a justfile with syntax inspired by make.
Unlike make, just is not a build system.

Building requires rust-opt (Rust 1.89 or newer). Cargo uses the supplied
vendor archive and Cargo.lock without downloading dependencies. Rust is
not required at runtime.

Run just --list to list recipes and just RECIPE to run one. Recipes use
sh by default; recipes using other interpreters need those installed.
Only run justfiles you trust, since recipes execute arbitrary commands.

The package includes a man page, Bash/Zsh/Fish completions, and examples
under /usr/doc/just-*/. Documentation: https://just.systems/man/en/
